      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Design a Voice — ZONOS3-Mini\n\n1. **First run:** just press Run. ZONOS3 downloads its voice server and model (about 1.7 GB, once) into `ComfyUI/models/zonos3` and starts by itself. Windows with an NVIDIA GPU.\n2. Pick a base voice in **ZONOS3 Voice**, or try a **preset** in Voice Design.\n3. Move the sliders: **Who** (gender, age, pitch, intonation), **Texture**, **Room**, **Delivery** and **Mood**. They stop where Zyphra measured the voice still sounds like the same person.\n4. Press **Run**.\n\n**Tips**\n- Mood and delivery are a nudge, not a guarantee: try two or three seeds.\n- Go easy when stacking Delivery and Mood: Liveliness, Happy and Chatty together raise the pitch a lot, so a deep voice can end up sounding like someone else.\n- *steer_hold* relaxes mood and delivery after ~4 seconds so long reads don't drift louder. Set 1 to keep them constant.\n- Want a cross between two voices? Swap **ZONOS3 Voice** for **ZONOS3 Voice Blend**."
      ]
    },
